From: Daniel Pawlik <pawlik.dan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: disable Pause advertising on RTL826x

RTL826x copper AN defaults to advertising Symmetric Pause (MMD 7.0x0010).
On hosts such as the Airoha AN7581 GDM4 path (Gemtek W1700K lan2), XFI
pause toward the PCS can be gated in the PCS driver, but copper pause
with the link partner still negotiates and stalls PHY transmit under
upload load. airoha_eth does not implement ethtool -A, so the partner
cannot keep pause forced off across reboot.

Clearing Pause only in rtl826x_get_features() is not enough: phylink
re-adds Pause to phydev->advertising from MAC pause capabilities before
config_aneg(). Also clear Pause/Asym_Pause from advertising in
rtl826x_config_aneg() immediately before genphy_c45_an_config_aneg(),
and drop them from supported in get_features().

Signed-off-by: Daniel Pawlik <pawlik.dan@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c | 10 +++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c	2026-10-11 13:02:20.983739648 +0200
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c	2026-10-11 13:02:21.004340942 +0200
@@ -3175,6 +3175,10 @@
 	linkmode_clear_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_10baseT_Full_BIT,
 			   phydev->supported);
 
+	/* See rtl826x_config_aneg() - strip Pause from the PHY feature set. */
+	linkmode_clear_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_Pause_BIT, phydev->supported);
+	linkmode_clear_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_Asym_Pause_BIT, phydev->supported);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -3209,6 +3213,14 @@
 	if (phydev->autoneg == AUTONEG_DISABLE)
 		return genphy_c45_pma_setup_forced(phydev);
 
+	/* Phylink/MAC often re-adds Pause into advertising from
+	 * mac_capabilities even after get_features() cleared it. Force it
+	 * off before programming C45 AN so copper pause cannot negotiate
+	 * and stall TX under load (W1700K lan2 / GDM4 USXGMII).
+	 */
+	linkmode_clear_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_Pause_BIT, phydev->advertising);
+	linkmode_clear_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_Asym_Pause_BIT, phydev->advertising);
+
 	ret = genphy_c45_an_config_aneg(phydev);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
